  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI, ResNet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 acc. The image modality clearly contributes meaningfully in fusion (RNA-only transformer at 0.653 → multimodal weighted at 0.713, a +0.06 gain), yet we have only tested ResNet50 as the image encoder, which performed very weakly in isolation (0.208). The key uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) can further improve the fused representation. Config_039 changes only the image encoder from ResNet50 to ViT-L while keeping all other proven-optimal settings (scVI, multiprofile, transformer, weighted), isolating the effect of image encoder quality. This is the highest-value experiment: if ViT-L helps, we find a new best; if not, we confirm ResNet50 is sufficient and retain config_033 as our answer. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, a clean single-variable test on the most impactful untested dimension is the best use of budget."
}

